    {
      "sender": "SYSTEM",
      "recipient": "USER",
      "content": "{{USER_INSTRUCTION}}ROUND 1 [provide: image_1, image_2, image_3]\nQuery: Look at the 5 tips at the bottom of the first infographic and the 8 steps in the third one. Check my 'Marketing Campaign' project in Todoist and add any of those items that aren't already there as new tasks.\nInstructions: Ask the assistant to cross-reference the 5 tips at the bottom of the first image and the 8 steps in the third image with your existing 'Marketing Campaign' project in Todoist. Instruct it to add any items from those lists that are currently missing as new tasks. If the assistant asks for clarification on which text to use, direct it to the numbered lists in those specific images. Once the assistant confirms it has added the missing tasks, proceed to the next round.\n\nROUND 2\nQuery: Actually, priorities just shifted to the pitch deck. Please delete all those marketing tasks you just added. Instead, look at the 6 main section headers in the second infographic. Cross-reference those with my 'Sales Pitch' project and add any missing sections as new tasks.\nInstructions: Tell the assistant that you've changed your mind because priorities shifted to the pitch deck. Ask it to undo the previous action by deleting the tasks it just created in the 'Marketing Campaign' project. Then, instruct it to cross-reference the 6 main section headers from the second infographic with your 'Sales Pitch' project, adding any missing sections as new tasks. If the assistant needs help finding the headers in the second image, mention they are the large titles with green and grey backgrounds. End the conversation once the assistant confirms the new tasks have been added.\n\nYou have 3 images available to share with the agent using the send_message_with_image tool.\nIMPORTANT: Image IDs are ZERO-INDEXED integers (0, 1, 2, ...). Do NOT add 1 to the IDs.\nAvailable image IDs: [0, 1, 2]\nImage mapping:\n  image_1.jpg -> image ID 0\n  image_2.jpg -> image ID 1\n  image_3.jpg -> image ID 2"
    },
